<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles II of Navarre</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1332">1332</a>–<a href="/years/1387">1387</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Charles the Bad</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles II, called the Bad, was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a> from 1349 and count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/evreux">Évreux</a>, a grandson of Louis X of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> through his mother Joan II. Holding large lands in Normandy, he intrigued against John II and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a> of France, switching between the English and French during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a>, and had the constable Charles de la Cerda murdered in 1354. Charles V's armies seized most of his Norman lands.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-ii-of-navarre.jpg" alt="Charles II of Navarre" width="320" height="369" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Charles_II_of_Navarre.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
